======================================================================
PRESPECIFIED SENSITIVITY DOMAINS
======================================================================

1. Fiber-orientation sensitivity

Documented perturbation:
    ±15 degrees

Purpose:
Assess robustness of predicted myocardial mechanical response to
variation in transmural fiber orientation.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

2. Material-parameter sensitivity

Documented perturbation:
    ±20%

Purpose:
Assess robustness of mechanical response to uncertainty in myocardial
material stiffness/constitutive parameters.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

3. Basal-boundary-condition sensitivity

Documented perturbation:
    ±20% or predefined alternative basal constraint,
    according to the finalized execution design.

Purpose:
Assess dependence of model response on basal mechanical constraint.

---------------------------------------------------------------------

4. Cavity-pressure sensitivity

Documented perturbation:
    ±10%

Purpose:
Assess sensitivity of model response to uncertainty in ventricular
loading pressure.

